From 62b911e5603ed74b49b21cb320a2ca29f15020a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ryan R. Fox" <ryanRfox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 16:25:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 039/110] feat(config): per-role effort level in cost-tier
 system (#3545)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* feat(config): add per-role effort level to cost-tier system

Add role_effort config to TownSettings and RigSettings, parallel to
role_agents. Cost-tier presets now include per-role effort defaults:
- standard: all high
- economy: workers high, patrol low, mayor/refinery medium
- budget: workers medium, all others low

AgentEnv resolves effort internally via ResolveRoleEffort using role
context already available in AgentEnvConfig (Role, Rig, TownRoot).
No call-site changes required.

Deprecates CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL env var — effort is now configured
per-role through config, matching the pattern used for model selection.
A deprecation notice is emitted when the env var is detected.

Resolution chain: GT_COST_TIER ephemeral → rig role_effort → town
role_effort → "high" default.

Refs: gtn-mol-dst0

* fix(config): add [1m] suffix to sonnet preset for 1M context

Claude Code's --model sonnet resolves to 200K context because the
explicit --model flag bypasses the built-in plan-based auto-detection
that enables 1M on Max/Team plans. Adding the [1m] suffix to the
sonnet preset ensures roles using claude-sonnet get 1M context.
